00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:31.800
companies outside the US. And the final

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:33.760
fund is something called a bond fund,

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:35.880
which helps provide stability as they're

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:37.960
generally less volatile than stocks, and

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:40.280
can help smooth out the ups and downs of

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:41.800
the market. So, the question is, how do

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:44.920
you split your money between the three

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:47.040
funds? Well, that all depends on your

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:48.680
risk tolerance. An older investor who

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:52.400
wants to protect their wealth might go

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:56.760
for a split like this: 35% US stocks,

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:58.440
25% international stocks, and 40% bonds.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:02.760
A middle-aged investor might choose

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:06.200
this: 45% US stocks, 30% international

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:10.200
stocks, and 25% bonds. A young moderate

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:14.400
risk investor might opt for this: 55% US

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:16.839
stocks, 35% international stocks, and

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:20.960
10% bonds. And a young aggressive

00:11:16.839 --> 00:11:25.080
investor might do this: 60% US stocks,

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:27.600
40% international stocks, and oh,

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:29.440
no bonds. Notice how this mostly depends

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:31.560
on your age. That's because younger

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:34.040
people have longer to stay invested if

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.880
there's a market crash. Historically,

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:38.240
with this kind of portfolio, you have

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:40.560
time to wait these out. Then, you come

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:42.320
out stronger than before. However, if

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.400
you're forced to sell for retirement,

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:46.160
you could end up making a loss. That's

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:48.720
why, in my opinion, it's actually

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:50.160
riskier not to take calculated risks

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.840
while you're young. So, hopefully, you

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:54.240
now know what kind of investing

