00:19:25.913 --> 00:19:27.933
>> [music]

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:31.920
>> So, most people focus on when to buy

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:34.400
stocks, but knowing when to sell [music]

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:36.160
is just as important, maybe even more.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:38.240
The thing is, selling usually goes

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:40.320
against our instincts. When prices start

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:43.240
dropping, we tell ourselves it'll bounce

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:45.320
back or it's just a paper loss. And when

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:47.240
prices are rising, we hesitate because

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:49.240
we don't want to sell too soon and miss

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:51.200
out on more. Even Warren Buffett, who

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:53.640
famously says his favorite holding

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:55.560
period is forever, has sold stocks when

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:58.080
the time was right. I like to joke that

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:59.920
my sell button is broken. But when I do

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:01.720
sell, there's always a good reason

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:03.560
behind it. I've made millions in the

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:05.280
markets, and one thing I've learned is

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:07.320
that holding onto a stock for the wrong

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.800
reasons can cost you just as much as

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.560
buying the wrong stock in the first

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:12.800
place. So, if you're serious about

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:14.720
investing, you'll need a clear strategy

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:16.240
for when to take profits, protect your

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:18.320
money, and move into better

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:20.760
opportunities. Here are three main

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:23.400
reasons when selling makes sense. Reason

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:25.680
one is if momentum is dying. Stocks move

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:27.720
based on three types of value. First,

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:29.600
there's fundamental value, which is what

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:31.920
the business is actually worth based on

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:34.040
real numbers like assets, revenue, and

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:36.440
profits. This is the value investors

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:38.320
like me look at when deciding if a stock

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:40.120
is a good long-term investment. Then

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:42.160
there's trading value, which is how the

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:44.360
market prices a stock based on

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:46.400
short-term supply and demand, trading

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:48.320
volume, and price patterns. It's less

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:50.040
about what the company is actually worth

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:52.160
and more about how traders react to

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:54.400
price movements. This is where technical

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:57.080
analysis comes into play. Traders look

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:58.520
at charts, trends, and historical data

00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:00.720
to predict where the stock will move

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:02.520
next. A stock's price can temporarily

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.680
rise or fall, not because the company

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:06.840
changed, but because traders are making

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:08.920
moves based on technical signals. And

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:11.360
finally, there's momentum value, which

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:13.800
is driven by hype, trends, and emotions.

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:15.600
This is when a stock's price skyrockets,

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:17.760
not because of solid fundamentals or

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:19.600
technical patterns, but because everyone

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:21.520
is talking about it. But why does this

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:23.360
matter? Well, if a stock is mostly

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:25.880
running on momentum rather than real

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:28.480
value, its price is fragile. And when

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:30.560
the hype dies, so does the stock price.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:32.400
You can spot the risky momentum stocks

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.400
by looking at things like Google Trends

